# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file every tool that rewrites a file picks its own convention —
# PowerShell's Set-Content, python's open(), git-bash, the Unity importer — and
# TODO.md drifts between CRLF and LF from one commit to the next. That shows up
# as whole-file diffs, spurious merge conflicts, and encoding errors when a tool
# re-reads what another one wrote.
#
# Declaring the policy here fixes it at the repo level, which is more reliable
# than converting after the fact with dos2unix.

# --- text we edit with tooling: normalise to LF in the repo and on disk -------
*.md        text eol=lf
*.markdown  text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf
*.gpl       text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# --- Windows-native scripts must keep CRLF or they misbehave -----------------
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.sln       text eol=crlf

# --- C# / Unity ---------------------------------------------------------------
# ENABLED 2026-08-23 (TASK #0382) for *.asset ONLY, and deliberately without
# merge=unityyamlmerge.
#
# Why this one and not the rest. Unity writes LF; with no attribute git applied
# core.autocrlf and rewrote ProjectSettings/ProjectAuditorSettings.asset into a
# whole-file diff with ZERO content change. `git diff --numstat` and
# `--ignore-all-space --numstat` were both empty — a phantom diff, recurring
# after every Editor run, and exactly the case CLAUDE.md says to investigate
# rather than hand-fix. 25 tracked files, so the renormalise is bounded.
#
# merge=unityyamlmerge is omitted on purpose for *.asset: the driver merges
# Unity's YAML object graph, and a ProjectSettings .asset is a flat settings
# file that a normal text merge handles correctly.
*.asset     text eol=lf

# ALL ENABLED. The header that used to sit here said "STILL DISABLED" and
# listed *.unity and *.prefab — that was stale: the lines below were already
# active, and TASK #0383's closure note inherited the error. Corrected
# 2026-08-24 (TASK #0390).
#
# The unityyamlmerge driver IS now configured — TASK #0390:
#   git config merge.unityyamlmerge.driver \
#     '"<Editor>/Data/Tools/UnityYAMLMerge.exe" merge -h -p --force \
#      --fallback none %O %B %A %A'
#   git config merge.unityyamlmerge.recursive binary
#
# ⚠️ That config lives in .git/config, which is NOT tracked. Every clone and
# every machine must set it independently. Without it git falls back to a
# plain text merge on scene files, which silently produces a corrupt scene
# rather than a conflict. Argument order matters: %O %B %A %A is base, theirs,
# ours, output — swapping %A and %B inverts the merge.
#
# *.prefab currently matches ZERO tracked files (M1.prefab was deleted with
# TASK #0348). The rule is kept because prefabs will return, not because it
# does anything today.
*.cs        text eol=lf
*.csproj    text eol=lf
*.unity     text eol=lf merge=unityyamlmerge
*.prefab    text eol=lf merge=unityyamlmerge
*.meta      text eol=lf

# --- binary: never diff, never normalise -------------------------------------
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.tga       binary
*.psd       binary
*.aseprite  binary
*.ase       binary
*.wav       binary
*.mp3       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.fbx       binary
*.blend     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.dll       binary
*.pdf       binary
